n  happen every time  because we  absolutely with clothes with shoes  with  our  [Music]  baggage for  south  for something yeah  well it's lucky that you were in the  corridor a lot of people in these  apartments are actually sleeping in  their corridors precisely because  they're afraid of an attack like this  well that's a situation in the capital  cave but odessa is one of the cities  along the southern coast that's still  under you can ukrainian control but the  russian military is approaching our  correspondent  hamid is there um talk to us about what  things are like in this city  well certainly you can see from the  picture  behind me here this is a fortified city  this is a city that has actually  been hit on the first night of the war  on february 24th 20 people died  on that day  and it is a city that president vladimir  zedenski had warned more than once that  russia is planning to attack it is a  very strategic port city on the black  sea one of the most important ports  for ukraine a lot of uh exports happen  from that city and as you mentioned uh  there is a russian advance to the south  of odessa and the russian uh troops are  still stuck in nico mikalayev but that's  only about 130 kilometers from here now  the ukrainians say that at the moment  they controlled the n24 which is the  road that would lead from nicolaive to  odessa but odessa as odessa feels that  it's not under pressure from this  advance from the south uh they could  there's also the fact that it's facing  the black sea the the ukrainians are  saying that the russians are fortifying  or building up their navel positions in  the sea that the the city could be  attacked from the sea as well and then  some do also say that a third front  could be open from across the border in  moldova from that breakaway region of  transnistria which is of course  pro-russian so  it's a city that feels that it could  become very quickly under siege and it's  actually throughout my travels in this  coun